            <tr><td colspan=2><hr></td></tr>
            <tr>
               <td colspan=2><img src="../images/spacer.gif" height="10" style="display:block">Think about it - currently your credit card users can refer others to get a small bonus.<br><br>
                   But now they would have the incentive to generate substantial cash back from finance charges of other users, which cascades 2 levels into their referrals.  Meaning a user gets cash back from two levels:<br><br>
                   
                   (A) Those he/she refers sign up and carry a balance, and<br>
                   (B) Those referred by his/her referred users who sign up and carry a balance.<br><br>
                   
                   So in other words, this is the first time that credit card users can get a (extremely minute) <b>share of the bank's profits</b> by referring others. ALL 100% FREE.<br><br>
                   
                And it's a win-win situation because the bank also expands its user base (and revenue from finance charges) from such referrals. And the more the finance charges generated by such users (thro balance transfers or remaining balance), the more the bank's revenue!</td></tr>
